From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 09:13:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 44/58] Question view returns the result only to full viewers
 (K1b)

When a question resolves, the engine stores its summary, gate_notes (the
competing pair and the verification_competing texts), the verification outcome
and target claim, the deferred follow-up texts and the claim and conflict ids in
questions.result. QuestionService.view() returned it unredacted, so it reached a
holder owner who was only routed the question through detail(), list() and
needs_input.

view() now replaces the result for a principal without full view with its
content-free subset (outcome, timed_out_routes); the key stays present. Askers,
full viewers, system principals and internal callers without a principal are
unchanged.

Regression tests (REVIEWER-2 probe P7): the stored result holds the content, a
routed-only owner sees only the outcome through detail() and needs_input lists,
and a full viewer, the asker and internal callers still get the whole result.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QgQYqiZ8KjrbuXgxGadraA
